description = "Ikemen GO, the open source M.U.G.E.N-compatible fighting game engine. Load the folder of an Ikemen GO installation, or any file inside it (data/system.def works), and the engine runs from there. Configuration and stats (hiscores, unlocks) persist in the frontend's save directory under ikemen/<pack>; replays stay in the content folder's save/ directory."
notes = "The core renders in its own GL context, outside the frontend's. The default build opens a hidden desktop-GL window, so it needs a display server (or SDL's offscreen video driver), and hands frames over as a software framebuffer. The IKEMEN_GLES=1 build instead renders GL ES 3.0 into a windowless EGL context, which is what a KMS/DRM frontend needs since it already holds the DRM master, and shares each finished frame with the frontend on the GPU (hardware rendering, dma-buf); when the frontend declines it falls back to the software framebuffer. Player 1-4 map to RetroPad ports 1-4; the keyboard is forwarded as well, so the engine's own input configuration screens work."
